The '''[[2025–26 in Scottish football|2025–26 season]]''' was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 132nd season of competitive football.

==Pre-season and friendlies==
Celtic faced [[Queen's Park F.C.|Queen's Park]] and [[Cork City F.C.|Cork City]] in early July.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2025/june/10/celtic-line-up-pre-season-friendly-against-queen-s-park/ | title=Celtic line up pre-season friendly against Queen's Park | publisher=Celtic FC | date=10 June 2025 | access-date=10 June 2025 | archive-date=10 June 2025 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250610123351/https://www.celticfc.com/news/2025/june/10/celtic-line-up-pre-season-friendly-against-queen-s-park/ | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2025/march/03/celtic-fc-to-compete-in-the-inaugural-cork-super-cup-this-summer/ | title=Celtic to compete in the inaugural Cork Super Cup this summer | publisher=Celtic FC | date=3 March 2025 | access-date=26 May 2025 | archive-date=3 March 2025 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250303225912/https://www.celticfc.com/news/2025/march/03/celtic-fc-to-compete-in-the-inaugural-cork-super-cup-this-summer/ | url-status=live }}</ref> They then travelled to Portugal for a pre-season training camp, where they played [[C.F. Estrela da Amadora|Estrela da Amadora]] and [[Sporting CP]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2025/june/24/ticket-information-for-the-celts--2025-26-pre-season-fixtures/ | title=Ticket information for the Celts' 2025/26 pre-season fixtures | publisher=Celtic FC | date=24 June 2025 | access-date=26 June 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2025/june/09/celtic-to-play-sporting-cp-in-pre-season-friendly/ | title=Celtic to play Sporting CP in pre-season friendly | publisher=Celtic FC | date=9 June 2025 | access-date=9 June 2025 | archive-date=10 June 2025 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250610093213/https://www.celticfc.com/news/2025/june/09/celtic-to-play-sporting-cp-in-pre-season-friendly/ | url-status=live }}</ref> On returning to Glasgow, the Scottish champions faced [[Newcastle United F.C.|Newcastle United]] at Celtic Park.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2025/may/06/celtic-to-take-on-newcastle-united-in-adidas-trophy-at-celtic-park/ | title=Celtic to take on Newcastle United in adidas Trophy at Celtic Park | publisher=Celtic FC | date=6 May 2025 | access-date=26 May 2025 | archive-date=7 May 2025 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250507080929/https://www.celticfc.com/news/2025/may/06/celtic-to-take-on-newcastle-united-in-adidas-trophy-at-celtic-park/ | url-status=live }}</ref> Their pre-season schedule concluded with a mini tournament in Italy, where they played [[AFC Ajax|Ajax]] and [[Al-Ahli Saudi FC|Al-Ahli]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://comofootball.com/en/como-cup-fixtures-announced/ | title=Como Cup Fixtures Announced! | publisher=Como 1907 | date=10 June 2025 | access-date=10 June 2025 | archive-date=14 June 2025 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250614004010/https://comofootball.com/en/como-cup-fixtures-announced/ | url-status=live }}</ref>

