|attendance = 59,079
|referee    = [[Don Robertson (referee)|Don Robertson]]
|result     = W
|note       = Celtic fans invaded the pitch after the third goal in the 98th minute, causing confusion over the end of the match. While a statement from Hearts said that "nobody seemed to know" whether it had ended, the [[Scottish Professional Football League|SPFL]] later confirmed that the referee had ended the match and had consulted with the Hearts coach prior to doing so.<ref name="SFA">{{cite web | title=Celtic v Heart of Midlothian | website=Scottish FA | date=2026-05-21 | url=https://www.scottishfa.co.uk/news/scottish-fa-statement-celtic-v-heart-of-midlothian/?rid=13929 | access-date=2026-05-21}}</ref> During the pitch invasion, Hearts players and staff were alleged to have been physically and verbally assaulted; they were escorted out of Celtic Park and unable to fulfil media commitments on personnel safety grounds.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Campbell |first1=Jordan |last2=Millar |first2=Colin |date=2026-05-16 |title= Hearts condemn ‘menacing and threatening atmosphere’ at Celtic in SPFL title loss |url= https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7284500/2026/05/16/hearts-celtic-scottish-premiership-title/ |access-date=2026-05-16 |website=The Athletic |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last1=Pirie |first1=Mark |last2=Farr |first2=Jacob |date=2026-05-16 |title= Hearts players 'assaulted' and escorted down tunnel after Celtic fans invade pitch|url= https://www.edinburghlive.co.uk/news/edinburgh-news/hearts-players-assaulted-escorted-down-33959265 |access-date=2026-05-16 |website=edinburghlive.co.uk|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-05-16 |title= SPFL 'utterly condemns' pitch invasion at Celtic Park|url= https://www.glasgowtimes.co.uk/sport/26114056.spfl-utterly-condemns-pitch-invasion-celtic-park/|access-date=2026-05-17 |website=glasgowtimes.co.uk|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-05-16 |title= Celtic 3-1 Hearts: Visitors say players, staff suffer 'serious physical and verbal abuse' after 'disgraceful' Celtic Park pitch invasion|url= https://www.skysports.com/football/news/11095/13544702/celtic-3-1-hearts-visitors-say-players-staff-suffer-serious-physical-and-verbal-abuse-after-disgraceful-celtic-park-pitch-invasion|access-date=2026-05-16 |website=edinburghlive.co.uk|language=en-GB}}</ref> [[Police Scotland]] later confirmed that they had received no complaints from Hearts regarding the reported allegations.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-05-28 |title= Police received no assault complaints from Hearts after Celtic match|url= https://www.glasgowtimes.co.uk/sport/26148106.police-received-no-assault-complaints-hearts-celtic-match/|access-date=2026-05-31 |website=glasgowtimes.co.uk|language=en-GB}}</ref>
}}

==Scottish Cup==
{{Main|2025–26 Scottish Cup}}
On 30 November, Celtic were drawn to face [[Auchinleck Talbot F.C.|Auchinleck Talbot]] in the fourth round of the [[2025–26 Scottish Cup]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cgmn1lnkrw4o | title=Scottish Cup: Celtic face Auchinleck Talbot in Scottish Cup with Aberdeen drawn against Raith Rovers | publisher=BBC Sport | date=30 November 2025 | access-date=4 December 2025}}</ref> On 18 January 2026, Celtic were drawn to face [[Dundee F.C.|Dundee]] at Celtic Park in the fifth round.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2026/january/18/celtic-face-home-tie-against-dundee-in-scottish-cup-fifth-round/ | title=Celtic face home tie against Dundee in Scottish Cup fifth round | publisher=Celtic FC | date=18 January 2026 | access-date=22 January 2026}}</ref> On 8 February, Celtic were drawn to face [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]] in the quarter-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2026/february/08/celtic-face-scottish-cup-quarter-final-derby-clash-at-ibrox/ | title=Celtic face Scottish Cup quarter-final derby clash at Ibrox | publisher=Celtic FC | date=8 February 2026 | access-date=8 February 2026}}</ref> On 8 March, Celtic were drawn to face [[St Mirren F.C.|St Mirren]] in the semi-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2026/march/08/Celtic-drawn-against-St-Mirren-in-Scottish-Cup-semi-final/ | title=Celtic drawn against St Mirren in Scottish Cup semi-final | publisher=Celtic FC | date=8 March 2026 | access-date=8 March 2026}}</ref> Celtic faced [[Dunfermline Athletic F.C.|Dunfermline Athletic]] in the final on 23 May.

